### :param divisor_low: The low 64 bits of the real divisor.
### :param divisor_high: The high 64 bits of the real divisor.
### :returns: The result.
### :throws: Crashes with `DivisionByZeroError` when a nonzero part is divided by zero, with `NumericDomainError` when a
###     quotient is NaN, or with `NumericOverflowError` when one is infinite.
@export("ingrid_c256_div_real")
@inline
routine c256_div_real(real_low: U64, real_high: U64, imag_low: U64, imag_high: U64,
    divisor_low: U64, divisor_high: U64) -> C256
    z: C256 = C256.from_halves(real_low, real_high, imag_low, imag_high)
    return z.truediv_real(b128_from_halves(low: divisor_low, high: divisor_high))

### The negation, for C256.neg.
### :param real_low: The low 64 bits of the real part.
### :param real_high: The high 64 bits of the real part.
